1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,360
Hi, and welcome to the CRM Scoring Podcast.

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:09,380
Every sales team has the same problem, too many leads and not enough hours.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,640
So someone has to decide who gets the first call.

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,360
In most teams, that decision is made by gut feeling

5
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:19,500
or by whoever spoke loudest in the last meeting.

6
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:22,520
Today I want to show you a simpler way.

7
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:26,780
It's called lead scoring. Let's scoring means giving

8
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:31,060
every lead a number so you can sort your list from the most promising to the least.

9
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:33,180
Two things go into that number.

10
00:00:34,380 --> 00:00:37,840
The first is fit. Does this company look like your best customers?

11
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,640
Think about the industry, the size of the company,

12
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,180
the country, and the job title of the person you're talking to.

13
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:49,380
A marketing director at a 200 person software company might be a perfect fit.

14
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:52,900
A student downloading a free guide probably isn't.

15
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:58,200
The second is intent. Is this lead showing interest right now?

16
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:04,300
Did they visit your pricing page? Open your emails, ask for a demo, reply to a message?

17
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,980
Fit tells you who could buy. Intent tells you who might buy soon.

18
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:12,480
Put the two together and you get three groups.

19
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:17,420
Hot leads fit well and are active now. Call them today.

20
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:23,240
Warm leads fit but they're quiet or they're active but not a perfect fit.

21
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:27,340
Keep them warm with useful emails and check back in a couple of weeks.

22
00:01:28,480 --> 00:01:33,180
Cold leads don't fit and aren't active. Don't spend your best hours on them.

23
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:37,620
Here's a simple way to start tomorrow. Take your CRM export.

24
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:42,280
Give each lead up to 50 points for fit and up to 50 for intent.

25
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:48,280
For fit, 10 points for the right industry, 10 for the right company size,

26
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:52,680
10 for a decision maker job title. For intent,

27
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:58,980
20 points for a visit to your pricing page, 20 for a demo request, 10 for a reply.

28
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:06,180
Anything over 70 is hot. 40 to 70 is warm. Below 40 is cold.

29
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,600
It won't be perfect but it will already be better than guessing.

30
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:13,580
Now three mistakes to avoid.

31
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:21,560
One, scoring only on fit. A perfect company that hasn't touched your website in a year is not hot.

32
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:28,240
Two, never updating the scores. A lead score should change when their behavior changes.

33
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:34,540
Three, hiding the reason. If a salesperson can't see why a lead is hot,

34
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:37,580
they won't trust the number and they'll go back to gut feeling.

35
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:42,100
That last point is exactly why we built CRM scoring.

36
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:47,700
You upload your CRM export and every lead gets hot, warm or cold,

37
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,420
together with a short explanation in plain words.

38
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:54,880
Why this lead and why now? It can send results back to Salesforce

39
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:58,680
and send a Slack alert the moment a lead turns hot.

40
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:02,380
You can try it free at CRMScoring.com.

41
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:05,660
There's also a free lead scoring template on the site,

42
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,560
so you can start with a spreadsheet today.

43
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,920
That's it for this episode.

44
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:14,760
Next time, we'll talk about the signals that tell you a lead is ready to buy.

45
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:18,180
Thanks for listening and good luck with your calls.
